        <mxCell id="lyE6EhfwZzf6AAQuFgmy-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#b85450;fillColor=#f8cecc;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="needs another Factor FACE AUTH" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="140" x="1450" y="740" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lyE6EhfwZzf6AAQuFgmy-4" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;ul style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web (West European)&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; text-align: start; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); direction: ltr;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; direction: ltr;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Passwordless approach:&lt;/b&gt; Switching to a passwordless authentication approach.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;div role=&quot;presentation&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit; direction: ltr;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Native authentication and Universal Login:&lt;/b&gt; For native applications, does it make sense to use the Universal Login screen or use the embedded login screens?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;div role=&quot;presentation&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px; font: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; color: inherit; direction: ltr;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Native Passkeys:&lt;/b&gt; Is it possible to incorporate native passkeys as part of the enrolment process, it looks that this is only allowed through the WebView? We would also like to understand the implications of combining native passkeys with those used through the web view in Universal Login Screen, particularly how the flow would work when passkeys are used as part of MFA or login screen using the native flow.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; direction: ltr;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Custom flow and CIBA:&lt;/b&gt; I would like to revisit the custom flow I shared with you previously to ensure that we are adhering to the appropriate standards, as well as review our CIBA flow.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="690" y="980" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qsvXYREZ0kHnVu0nIN_h-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#82b366;fillColor=#d5e8d4;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="We do not need a second MFA for Guardian Enrollment" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="240" x="1200" y="965" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
